{"id": "EUVD-2026-81866", "enisaUuid": "5306782c-633d-3174-ba00-0590eb61a3ab", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncoresight: etm4x: missing cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() in perf enable\n\nIn the perf enable path, there are missing cases where\ncscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() is not called:\n\n  - Branch broadcast is selected but not supported by the hardware\n  - etm4_enable_hw() fails\n\nThis can lead to a leak of config_desc->active_cnt.\nFix this by properly calling cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config()\nin these error paths.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba63c62d4252f6bc58fd2a567075c72d03332562", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26f9e89bad5a7e3005d3dc97a2e2fa6d6b2b8bb6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d5f3dae82705d9388434892915008da3bb83c4ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7e4f2702bbadbde887a5d8897297720a7f037ee5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a47f0be6557b4a851addd430383a4dc7ee08752"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90273", "GHSA-24qc-78x7-rfr3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04c46e58-7494-3531-9a00-290d32359bbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2aa8ed1d-fb25-3216-872c-df3f760d096b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "32c525c7-275e-324a-bf08-a5c9f6575844", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "810ac401db1fe432020d7936a199591000de8279 <ba63c62d4252f6bc58fd2a567075c72d03332562"}, {"id": "8469c938-29de-38a5-9881-a365d7518e3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "941086d1-df60-379c-bcff-cfea1b40aa2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "810ac401db1fe432020d7936a199591000de8279 <26f9